te change divided by the 2016 rate, multiplied by 100.\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Analyses were conducted using SAS (version 9.4; SAS Institute) to account for HCUP’s complex survey design and weighting.\"}], \"confidence\": \"high\", \"uncertain_fields\": []}", "type": "text"}]}